WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.367
-Welcome to
"The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:02.367 --> 00:00:03.767
You're here.
You made it.

00:00:03.767 --> 00:00:07.200
Thank you for watching at home.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:08.567
Let's get to some news.

00:00:08.567 --> 00:00:10.767
Well, guys,
due to Hurricane Ian,

00:00:10.767 --> 00:00:13.334
the January 6th Committee
just postponed

00:00:13.334 --> 00:00:16.367
its public hearing that was
scheduled for tomorrow.

00:00:16.367 --> 00:00:18.767
Yeah, all day, Trump was praying
for a rain delay

00:00:18.767 --> 00:00:20.634
like a pitcher facing
Aaron Judge.

00:00:20.634 --> 00:00:22.367
Like, "Please."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:22.367 --> 00:00:24.067
Yep, the hearing is postponed.

00:00:24.067 --> 00:00:26.167
This morning Trump woke up
like Kevin in "Home Alone."

00:00:26.167 --> 00:00:28.033
He's like,
"I made my hearing disappear."

00:00:28.033 --> 00:00:29.534
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.534 --> 00:00:31.734
Some political news --
Senator Bernie Sanders said

00:00:31.734 --> 00:00:33.868
that he hasn't yet decided
whether he will run

00:00:33.868 --> 00:00:37.033
for president again in 2024.

00:00:37.033 --> 00:00:38.901
People were like,
"President of what?"

00:00:38.901 --> 00:00:40.968
[ Laughter ]

00:00:40.968 --> 00:00:42.834
Yep, Bernie
still hasn't decided.

00:00:42.834 --> 00:00:44.000
Meanwhile everyone else is like,

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:46.033
"How many times
do we have to decide this?

00:00:46.033 --> 00:00:48.167
No."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.167 --> 00:00:49.567
Right now, Biden is thinking,

00:00:49.567 --> 00:00:51.534
"Please run so I look like
the hot, young stud. Please."

00:00:51.534 --> 00:00:53.634
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.634 --> 00:00:55.100
Yeah, well,
ahead of midterm elections,

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:58.300
House GOP Leader Kevin McCarthy
and other House Republicans

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:00.734
put out a new ad
promoting their agenda.

00:01:00.734 --> 00:01:03.400
But there was one problem --
some of the footage in the ad

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:04.634
that was supposed to be America

00:01:04.634 --> 00:01:06.367
was actually footage
from Russia.

00:01:06.367 --> 00:01:08.400
[ Laughter ]
That's real.

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:09.667
And that wasn't
the only mistake.

00:01:09.667 --> 00:01:11.167
Take a look at this spot.

00:01:26.334 --> 00:01:27.567
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.801 --> 00:01:31.734
-Yeah, there's so many --
-Wow!

00:01:31.734 --> 00:01:33.367
Not even close.
-Riddled.

00:01:33.367 --> 00:01:36.167
Riddled with errors.

00:01:36.167 --> 00:01:38.467
-Speaking of Russia,
I just heard they announced

00:01:38.467 --> 00:01:41.400
they're boycotting
next year's Oscars.

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:43.367
Mm, that's a tough break
for Russia's biggest movie

00:01:43.367 --> 00:01:46.067
this year, "I Actually Have
A Lot to Worry About Darling."

00:01:46.067 --> 00:01:51.801
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.801 --> 00:01:54.467
You guys see this last night?
NASA intentionally crashed

00:01:54.467 --> 00:01:57.767
a spacecraft into an asteroid
to see if it could stop one

00:01:57.767 --> 00:02:00.534
coming towards Earth
in the future.

00:02:00.534 --> 00:02:02.801
Go, NASA.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.801 --> 00:02:04.400
Meanwhile, the Space Force
was like, "Cool, cool.

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:06.200
So what exactly
is our role again?

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:08.200
Like, what -- what do we do?"
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:09.968
Hey, listen to this --
I heard that the CIA

00:02:09.968 --> 00:02:12.667
just launched its own podcast.

00:02:12.667 --> 00:02:14.901
The CIA was like, "After
75 years of listening to you,

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:17.534
now you can listen to us."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.534 --> 00:02:18.868
Well, guys,
everyone loves TikTok,

00:02:18.868 --> 00:02:20.334
but sometimes you just
want to skip through

00:02:20.334 --> 00:02:22.234
the boring parts of a video
and get right to the good part.

00:02:22.234 --> 00:02:24.300
Well, it turns out you can

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:25.467
with this new thing
that we're doing on our show.

00:02:25.467 --> 00:02:26.968
For instance,
if you're watching a video here,

00:02:26.968 --> 00:02:28.200
you can skip this part...

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:30.267
♪♪

00:02:30.267 --> 00:02:31.868
-...and go right to this part.

00:02:31.868 --> 00:02:34.234
♪♪

00:02:34.234 --> 00:02:38.167
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.167 --> 00:02:39.434
-Let me give you
another example.

00:02:39.434 --> 00:02:41.300
You can skip this part...

00:02:44.767 --> 00:02:46.434
and go right to this part.

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:49.200
[ Thuds ]

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:51.100
[ Audience "Ohhs" ]

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:53.033
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:53.033 --> 00:02:55.133
-The fish tank!

00:02:55.133 --> 00:02:57.300
The final example --
you can skip this part...

00:02:57.300 --> 00:03:01.033
-I'm doing a part two
to the treadmill video

00:03:01.033 --> 00:03:03.133
I did just recently.

00:03:03.133 --> 00:03:04.501
-Yeah, and just go
right to this part.

00:03:09.033 --> 00:03:10.334
[ Laughter ]
-There you go. Perfect.

00:03:10.334 --> 00:03:14.300
Just so you know
that's available.

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:16.200
Switching gears --
ahead of the holiday season,

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:20.400
Macy's announced plans to hire
more than 40,000 new workers.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:22.701
So divide that between
the remaining Macy's locations,

00:03:22.701 --> 00:03:24.701
and you have 40,000 per store.

00:03:24.701 --> 00:03:26.534
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.534 --> 00:03:29.901
Some more business news.
In an effort to fight theft,

00:03:29.901 --> 00:03:33.934
retailers like Home Depot
are now locking up items.

00:03:33.934 --> 00:03:35.801
That's right,
trust Home Depot on security

00:03:35.801 --> 00:03:37.467
when they can't even
keep birds out.

00:03:37.467 --> 00:03:40.801
[ Laughter ]

00:03:40.801 --> 00:03:44.067
Some TV news -- the other night,
there was a new --

00:03:44.067 --> 00:03:45.434
There's always birds
in Home Depot flying around.

00:03:45.434 --> 00:03:47.934
-Come on, there are.
"What's this bird doing in here?

00:03:47.934 --> 00:03:49.467
Come on.
It's not a bird store."

00:03:49.467 --> 00:03:52.367
-Some TV news -- the other night
there was an all-new episode

00:03:52.367 --> 00:03:55.033
of "Celebrity Wheel of Fortune,"
and one of the contestants --

00:03:55.033 --> 00:03:56.934
Snoop Dogg --
had a little trouble

00:03:56.934 --> 00:03:58.033
with some of the puzzles.

00:03:58.033 --> 00:04:00.234
This is real.
Check this out.

00:04:00.234 --> 00:04:03.734
[ Bell dings ]
-Snoop?

00:04:03.734 --> 00:04:05.767
-"Swallowing the -- the knot"?

00:04:05.767 --> 00:04:07.100
[ Laughter ]

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:08.367
-That --
no, that's not right.

00:04:08.367 --> 00:04:11.300
[ Bell dings ]
Snoop?

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:13.434
-"Airport teacher."
-No.

00:04:13.434 --> 00:04:16.100
[ Bell dings ]
And snoop?

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:17.234
"Toilet Atlas."

00:04:17.234 --> 00:04:19.934
[ Laughter ]
-I have no idea.

00:04:19.934 --> 00:04:22.934
[ Bell dings ]
-And it's Snoop.

00:04:22.934 --> 00:04:24.334
-"Baking onions."

00:04:24.334 --> 00:04:25.334
[ Laughter ]

00:04:25.334 --> 00:04:27.234
[ Rim shot ]

00:04:27.234 --> 00:04:32.567
[ Applause ]

00:04:32.567 --> 00:04:35.167
-Something was baked that night.
It wasn't onions on that one.

00:04:35.167 --> 00:04:36.567
[ Laughter ]

00:04:36.567 --> 00:04:37.868
Finally, guys, it is Tuesday.

00:04:37.868 --> 00:04:40.033
It's time for "WeTweet."
Here we go.

00:04:40.033 --> 00:04:43.801
-♪ WeTweet ♪

00:04:43.801 --> 00:04:45.100
♪♪

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:46.267
♪ WeTweet ♪

00:04:46.267 --> 00:04:48.534
-Welcome to "WeTweet"!

00:04:48.534 --> 00:04:51.167
This is where we,
as a group, decide something

00:04:51.167 --> 00:04:52.767
we should post on Twitter.

00:04:52.767 --> 00:04:53.968
I'm gonna show you
five different tweets,

00:04:53.968 --> 00:04:55.033
and we're all gonna vote

00:04:55.033 --> 00:04:56.667
on whether you
like each one or not.

00:04:56.667 --> 00:04:58.067
You all have voting clickers
at your seats?

00:04:58.067 --> 00:05:00.868
I see people scrambling
for them, sharing them.

00:05:00.868 --> 00:05:03.501
Everyone has their own,
so it's all gonna be fine.

00:05:03.501 --> 00:05:04.868
You can vote for all of them,

00:05:04.868 --> 00:05:06.267
you can vote for none of them,
whatever you want,

00:05:06.267 --> 00:05:07.667
and we'll see the results live.

00:05:07.667 --> 00:05:09.000
Higgins, you have your clicker?
-Got it.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:11.467
-All right.
Your thumb's already on no.

00:05:11.467 --> 00:05:12.734
-Well...
[ Laughter ]

00:05:12.734 --> 00:05:14.300
Wanna be positive.
-Why --

00:05:14.300 --> 00:05:15.434
-I wanna be positive.
-Yeah, but why --

00:05:15.434 --> 00:05:17.133
-I'm gonna put "no"
on every one.

00:05:17.133 --> 00:05:18.267
-What? You're gonna say no
to all of them?

00:05:18.267 --> 00:05:20.267
-Yep, just so it'll be fair.

00:05:20.267 --> 00:05:21.734
'Cause Tariq's --
Tariq's gonna go yes --

00:05:21.734 --> 00:05:23.634
-Tariq, what are you thinking?
-I voted -- I'm done.

00:05:23.634 --> 00:05:24.868
I voted "yes" to everything.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:24.868 --> 00:05:26.968
-All right. Quest,
I know you're very positive.

00:05:26.968 --> 00:05:28.334
You always vote yes.
-Always yes.

00:05:28.334 --> 00:05:29.534
-Yes.
-I love my job.

00:05:29.534 --> 00:05:32.133
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:32.133 --> 00:05:33.501
Whatever tweet
gets the most likes,

00:05:33.501 --> 00:05:35.467
we will tweet it out
live on the show,

00:05:35.467 --> 00:05:37.801
so that you can all like it
and "wetweet" it.

00:05:37.801 --> 00:05:40.200
-Nice.
-It's a shared experience.

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:43.200
You guys ready for this?
The first tweet is...

00:05:46.501 --> 00:05:48.200
[ Laughter ]

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:51.267
♪♪

00:05:51.267 --> 00:05:54.000
Some people laughing, some
people just stone-- stone-faced.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:56.367
-Yeah.
-I don't know.

00:05:56.367 --> 00:05:58.534
-Some people don't know they
should -- they shouldn't do --

00:05:58.534 --> 00:05:59.968
-Yeah, I don't think
it's gonna work.

00:05:59.968 --> 00:06:03.167
The votes are in.
Let's see the results.

00:06:03.167 --> 00:06:04.601
-Oh, oh.
-All right, not bad.

00:06:04.601 --> 00:06:06.567
Not bad. 100...

00:06:06.567 --> 00:06:08.501
Very honest audience.
I like that, yeah.

00:06:08.501 --> 00:06:09.834
-Lot of abstentions.
-Wasn't the -- yeah.

00:06:09.834 --> 00:06:10.901
Wasn't the best,
wasn't the worst.

00:06:10.901 --> 00:06:12.334
-Yeah. Wasn't worst.
Was fine.

00:06:12.334 --> 00:06:13.968
-Let's see this next one here.
It says...

00:06:17.901 --> 00:06:19.267
[ Laughter ]

00:06:19.267 --> 00:06:20.534
♪♪

00:06:20.534 --> 00:06:22.100
-Come on. That's true.
-That's rare.

00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:23.367
-That's fair.
-That's a rare sighting.

00:06:23.367 --> 00:06:24.801
-That's a rare baby name
nowadays.

00:06:24.801 --> 00:06:26.300
-Yeah, it's like "What --
What's the name of your baby?"

00:06:26.300 --> 00:06:27.501
"It's Cheryl."
-"Cheryl."

00:06:27.501 --> 00:06:28.968
-Yeah.
-Gladys.

00:06:28.968 --> 00:06:30.934
-All right, here we go.
You cast your votes.

00:06:30.934 --> 00:06:33.400
Let's see the results.

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:35.334
-Oh!
-Oh, barely better.

00:06:35.334 --> 00:06:37.801
♪♪

00:06:37.801 --> 00:06:39.367
-"Cheryl" --
-I love that -- barely better.

00:06:39.367 --> 00:06:40.934
We might not even
tweet one out tonight.

00:06:40.934 --> 00:06:42.534
Who knows?
[ Laughter ]

00:06:42.534 --> 00:06:43.601
Next one here says...

00:06:46.501 --> 00:06:49.067
Oh, that's interesting.
[ Audience groans ]

00:06:49.067 --> 00:06:52.400
That one got -- you can't --
you can't boo the jokes.

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:53.968
Just...
[ Laughter ]

00:06:53.968 --> 00:06:56.000
...thumbs up or thumbs down.
Please no booing.

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:57.167
-'90s George Carlin.
-I don't need any

00:06:57.167 --> 00:06:59.200
audible booing of jokes, yeah.

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:00.701
I don't even think
we need to wait.

00:07:00.701 --> 00:07:03.367
Let's just see the results.
This is gonna be a landslide.

00:07:03.367 --> 00:07:04.400
Yeah, okay.
[ Sad tuba ]

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:06.934
-Wow.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:06.934 --> 00:07:08.534
Wow.
-Wow.

00:07:08.534 --> 00:07:10.400
-Wow.

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:12.033
-Here we go.
This next one says...

00:07:17.434 --> 00:07:19.567
-I'm gonna say
this one's gonna win.

00:07:19.567 --> 00:07:23.367
-"It's not connecting,
it needs ink.

00:07:23.367 --> 00:07:27.133
Uh, honey, do we need to make
any more CD-ROM labels?"

00:07:27.133 --> 00:07:30.734
All right, here we go.
Let's see the results.

00:07:30.734 --> 00:07:32.033
-Oh!
-Oh!

00:07:32.033 --> 00:07:33.801
Squeaky, but very nice.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:33.801 --> 00:07:35.133
♪♪

00:07:35.133 --> 00:07:37.000
You're being very nice tonight.
-Wow.

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:38.234
-You're being a very giving
audience tonight.

00:07:38.234 --> 00:07:40.567
I appreciate that.
We're down to our last one.

00:07:40.567 --> 00:07:41.734
Here we go.
It says...

00:07:45.501 --> 00:07:46.701
[ Laughter ]

00:07:46.701 --> 00:07:48.400
Cast your vote.
This one...

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:50.667
I feel good -- I feel best
with this one.

00:07:50.667 --> 00:07:52.434
I think.
I don't know.

00:07:52.434 --> 00:07:54.000
All right.

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:55.467
I think everyone
cast their votes.

00:07:55.467 --> 00:07:57.234
We know if it's
gonna win or not.

00:07:57.234 --> 00:08:00.067
Let's see the results here.

00:08:00.067 --> 00:08:02.467
Whoa!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:02.467 --> 00:08:04.834
By far, by far!
Thank you!

00:08:04.834 --> 00:08:06.634
-Whoa!
-That was, by far, the winner!

00:08:06.634 --> 00:08:09.200
I'm gonna post this
during the commercial break.

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:10.934
If you see it on your feed,
give it a like,

00:08:10.934 --> 00:08:12.634
give it a "wetweet," and enjoy.

